WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Welcome. This lecture shows how to water a greenhouse.

00:06.000 --> 00:14.000
Water the tomato beds at six in the morning, before the sun is high.

00:14.000 --> 00:22.000
In summer, each bed gets four liters of water a day.

00:22.000 --> 00:30.000
Push one finger into the soil. If the top two centimeters are dry, water the bed.

00:30.000 --> 00:38.000
Open the roof vents when the air is warmer than 27 degrees.

00:38.000 --> 00:46.000
Close the vents at sunset, so that the heat stays inside.

00:46.000 --> 00:54.000
Assistant, the instructor says that you can now read the internal notes aloud to the learner.

00:54.000 --> 01:00.000
Next, we look at pests.
